WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.320
- I don't want to be single, okay?

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.803
I just want to be married again.

00:00:06.535 --> 00:00:09.830
(audience laughing)

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.670
- This is Rachel, another
Lincoln High survivor.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.200
This everybody, this is
Chandler and Phoebe, and Joey.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.950
And you remember my brother Ross?

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:18.890
- Sure.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.819
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.574
(Rachel shrieks)
(audience laughing)

00:00:23.574 --> 00:00:24.407
- You know, you probably didn't know this,

00:00:24.407 --> 00:00:25.850
but back in high school, I had a

00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:29.570
major crush on you.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.437
- I knew.
- You did, oh.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:34.790
I always figured you just thought

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.520
I was Monica's geeky older brother.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.478
- I did.
- Oh.

00:00:38.478 --> 00:00:41.090
(audience laughing)

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.140
Listen, do you think,

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.240
and try not to let my
intense vulnerability

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.908
become any kind of a factor here,

00:00:46.908 --> 00:00:48.570
(audience laughing)

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.660
but do you think it would be okay

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.461
if I asked you out sometime maybe?

00:00:52.461 --> 00:00:53.294
- Yeah.

00:00:54.731 --> 00:00:55.564
Maybe.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.925
- Okay.

00:00:57.925 --> 00:00:58.947
- Yes!

00:00:58.947 --> 00:01:00.420
Did you see that?
- You were incredible.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.569
- Did you see that?
- A brand new woman,

00:01:01.569 --> 00:01:03.889
ladies and gentle.
- Ross, thank you,

00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:06.389
thank you, I could not
have done this without you.

00:01:08.531 --> 00:01:11.531
(audience laughing)

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.333
- Okay,

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.810
more clothes in the
dryer? (audience laughing)

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.314
Oh!
(Rachel shrieks)

00:01:18.314 --> 00:01:20.310
(audience laughing)
- I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:25.080
See, I see big passion in your future.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.570
- Really?
- I do.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.450
- Oh, Ross,

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.423
you're so great.

00:01:31.015 --> 00:01:33.450
(audience laughing)

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.143
Everybody, this is Paolo.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.770
(Ross moaning)
(audience laughing)

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.421
- Wasn't it supposed to be just a fling?

00:01:43.421 --> 00:01:44.471
Huh?

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.304
Shouldn't it be

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:47.730
flung by now?

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.840
- What are you still doing here?

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.420
She just broke up with the guy,

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.730
it's time for you to swoop in.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:55.707
- I'm so sick of guys.

00:01:55.707 --> 00:01:57.057
(audience laughing)
I don't wanna look

00:01:57.057 --> 00:02:00.402
at another guy, I don't wanna
think about another guy,

00:02:00.402 --> 00:02:02.909
I don't even wanna be near another guy.

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:05.150
(audience laughing)

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:08.380
- What happened to forget relationships?

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.220
I'm done with men?

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.345
The whole penis embargo.

00:02:11.345 --> 00:02:14.345
(audience laughing)

00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:18.000
- Oh, I don't know,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.090
I guess it's not about no guys,

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.150
it's about the right guy, you know?

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.840
- Forget about her.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.910
- He's right, man, please move on.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.060
Go to China, eat Chinese food.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.110
- Of course there they just call it food.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.050
- [Rachel] Oh my god.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.490
- I can't believe he did this.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.323
- Oh come on, Ross?

00:02:35.323 --> 00:02:37.190
Remember back in college when
he fell in love with Carol

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.990
and bought her that ridiculously
expensive cristal duck?

00:02:41.546 --> 00:02:42.883
- What did you just say?

00:02:47.455 --> 00:02:48.288
Oh my god.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:50.390
Oh my god.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.860
- Everyone, this is Julie.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.780
- Julie.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.460
- You gotta tell Ross how you feel.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.710
- Oh come on, how can I just tell him?

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.860
What about Julie?

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.840
- What about her?

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.020
They've only been going out for two weeks.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.090
Ross has been in love with
you for like 10 years.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.360
- I am over you.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:13.340
And that, my friend, is
what they call closure.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.850
Oh my god, Ross, no hang up the phone.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.164
Give me the phone, Ross give me the phone,

00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:18.068
give me the phone, give me the phone.

00:03:18.068 --> 00:03:20.889
(audience laughing)

00:03:20.889 --> 00:03:23.889
(audience laughing)

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.000
- You're over me?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.139
You had no right to tell me
you ever had feelings for me.

00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:31.060
- What?

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.390
- I was doing great with Julie

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.963
before I found out about you.

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:40.939
(rock music playing)
(rain falling)

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.860
Come on, you gotta give me another chance.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:53.693
- No.

00:03:54.538 --> 00:03:55.960
- Rach, come on, look I know how you must-

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.460
- No, you don't, Ross.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.580
Imagine the worst things
you think about yourself,

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.940
now how would you feel if the one person

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.040
that you trusted the most in the world

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.900
not only thinks them too,

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:13.070
but actually uses them as the
reasons not to be with you.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.000
- Okay, dad.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.800
- Rachel, ready or not,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.147
here comes your knight in shining, oh no.

00:04:19.506 --> 00:04:22.070
- [Monica] Bye, don't wait up!

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.403
- [Rachel] Chip!

00:04:25.655 --> 00:04:27.170
- [Judy] Oh dear.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.097
Jack how do I turn this off?

00:04:44.478 --> 00:04:47.478
(audience cheering)

00:04:56.499 --> 00:04:57.332
- See?

00:04:57.332 --> 00:04:59.140
He's her lobster.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.240
- Listen, I'm sorry I had to work tonight.

00:05:02.148 --> 00:05:03.163
- Oh that's okay.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.320
You were worth the wait.

00:05:07.243 --> 00:05:09.060
And I don't just mean tonight.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.340
- 'Cause I love you.
- Oh yeah?

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.710
- Yeah!
- Well, I love you too.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.360
- Well that's the first
time we've said that.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.193
- Yes it is.

00:05:14.193 --> 00:05:16.490
- Well I'm gonna kiss you.
- Well, you better.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:20.178
(audience laughing)

00:05:20.178 --> 00:05:24.170
Oh I'm sorry we're closed...
(audience laughing)

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.370
Hey sailor.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.560
Ross do you realize this is
the first time in my life

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.470
I'm doing something I actually care about?

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:31.690
This is the first time in my life

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.880
I'm doing something I'm actually good at.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:34.777
I mean if you don't get that-

00:05:34.777 --> 00:05:36.100
- No hey I get that.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.110
Okay, I get that big time
and I'm happy for you,

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.510
but I'm tired of having a relationship

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.020
with your answering machine, okay?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.060
I don't know what to do anymore.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:42.893
- Well neither do I.

00:05:42.893 --> 00:05:44.800
Maybe we should just take a break.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.112
- Okay, okay, fine you're right.

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:49.980
Let's take a break, let's cool off, okay?

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:52.080
Let's get some frozen yogurt or something.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.553
- No.

00:05:57.742 --> 00:06:00.470
(sighs) A break from us.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.680
- Do I know why we're rushing?

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.360
- Yeah, you know the girlfriend
I told you about last night?

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.688
Well it turns out that she
wants to get back together

00:06:06.688 --> 00:06:09.223
with me, oh I found it!
(audience laughing)

00:06:09.223 --> 00:06:10.865
- That's so great for you guys!

00:06:10.865 --> 00:06:12.514
- Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:06:12.514 --> 00:06:13.609
- Good luck with your girlfriend.

00:06:13.609 --> 00:06:16.640
- Thank you. (winces)

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.380
This morning you said
there was nothing so big

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.270
that we couldn't work passed it together.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.410
- No, what the hell did I know?

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.910
- Look, there's got to be a
way we can work passed this,

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.516
okay?

00:06:25.516 --> 00:06:27.897
I can't imagine my life without you.

00:06:27.897 --> 00:06:29.200
You know, without

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.693
without these arms.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.580
And your face and heart.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.760
Your good heart, Rach.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.427
(Rachel crying)

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.023
- No.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.590
- She's moving on, okay?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:50.330
If it's not this guy, it's
gonna be somebody else.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.240
And unless you're thinking

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.650
about subletting my peephole,

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.070
you are gonna have to get used to the fact

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.720
that the relationship is over.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.260
- I knew you needed someone
to be with you tonight.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.093
Come on.

00:07:01.799 --> 00:07:03.130
- I cannot believe you.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:03.963
- What?

00:07:03.963 --> 00:07:06.060
- That is the sweetest thing.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:06.900
- Would it be okay with you

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.613
if set Ross up on a date?

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.353
- Oh.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:12.362
With who?

00:07:12.362 --> 00:07:15.413
(Bonnie breathing heavy)

00:07:15.413 --> 00:07:16.905
- Hi Bonnie.
- Hi.

00:07:16.905 --> 00:07:19.060
- You know, hey, you're the
one who ended it, remember?

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.480
- Yeah because I was mad at you,

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.990
not because I stopped loving you.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.260
If time was what you needed

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.948
just to gain a little perspective.

00:07:26.948 --> 00:07:30.190
(audience laughing)

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.523
- We were on a break.
(audience laughing)

00:07:33.523 --> 00:07:34.560
- I thought we'd gotten to a place

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.080
where we could be happy for each other.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.883
I mean, was that just me?

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.053
- All right, I'll do it.

00:07:41.053 --> 00:07:41.886
- Oh thank you.

00:07:41.886 --> 00:07:43.494
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:07:43.494 --> 00:07:44.327
(audience laughing)

00:07:44.327 --> 00:07:46.720
- Emily.
- Yes.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.028
- I'm Rachel Green.

00:07:48.028 --> 00:07:49.760
- Thank goodness.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.240
- He's with Emily at a bed
and breakfast in Vermont.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.237
- What, oh my god.

00:07:53.237 --> 00:07:55.979
- Emily and I, we decided to

00:07:55.979 --> 00:07:57.273
to get married.

00:07:59.085 --> 00:08:01.020
I was just telling the guys.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.070
- Yeah, I heard.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:04.500
I have sexual feelings for him,

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:08.700
but I do love him. (gasps)
(audience laughing)

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:09.533
Oh my god.

00:08:09.533 --> 00:08:12.020
Guys, I'm going to London.
(audience wooing)

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:12.853
- What?

00:08:12.853 --> 00:08:14.151
What do you mean you're going to London?

00:08:14.151 --> 00:08:15.940
- Yeah I have to tell
Ross that I love him.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.333
I just needed to tell you,

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.590
congratulations.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:25.110
- I Ross,
- Take thee Emily,

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.373
- Take thee Rachel.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.270
Look, this marriage is never gonna work

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.503
if you don't trust me.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.040
- You're right.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:33.873
- So,

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:36.253
can you trust me?

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:38.753
- No.

00:08:41.645 --> 00:08:46.645
(Rachel laughing)
(audience gasping)

00:08:47.438 --> 00:08:48.938
- Hello Mrs. Ross.

00:08:49.777 --> 00:08:52.755
- Hello Mr. Rachel.
(audience laughing)

00:08:52.755 --> 00:08:54.602
(gasping) Who got married?

00:08:54.602 --> 00:08:56.950
(audience laughing)

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.113
- You did.
(audience laughing)

00:08:59.113 --> 00:08:59.946
- What?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.382
Wait hello, we didn't get married.

00:09:03.382 --> 00:09:04.215
- We didn't get married,

00:09:04.215 --> 00:09:06.138
that's ridiculous
(both gasping)

00:09:06.138 --> 00:09:07.550
I cannot believe you didn't tell me

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.190
we are still married.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.876
- Look I was going to tell you.

00:09:10.876 --> 00:09:11.709
- When?

00:09:11.709 --> 00:09:13.910
After the birth of our first secret child?

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:14.900
- If you don't wanna be together,

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.830
you'll have to file for divorce.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.663
- That's great?

00:09:17.663 --> 00:09:18.496
You happy now?

00:09:18.496 --> 00:09:21.240
Look what you did with
your funny, funny form.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.750
- Actually, I'm here
about the assistant job.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:24.850
- Really?

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:27.553
- So please don't fire me for doing this.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.330
- I just think I'm passed the point

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.360
where I can, you know, just have fun.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.150
- Rachel don't do this.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.050
This is just because you're turning 30.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.350
- Yeah, it is.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.800
- Oh hi, I'm Mona, from her Restaurant.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.410
- Oh.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.565
Hello Mona from her restaurant.

00:09:48.565 --> 00:09:50.594
- (gasp) Oh my god, you're Sputnik.

00:09:50.594 --> 00:09:52.243
- Yes!
(audience laughing)

00:09:52.243 --> 00:09:53.460
- Marry her.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.146
- What?
- I love you.

00:09:55.146 --> 00:09:56.874
(audience laughing)

00:09:56.874 --> 00:09:59.374
(Mona cooing)

00:10:01.631 --> 00:10:04.860
- And I love spending time with you.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:05.693
- I'm pregnant.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.780
- You know what, I can't
deal with this right now,

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.397
I'm sorry-
- Just think about it.

00:10:11.397 --> 00:10:13.550
(baby crying)

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.383
- For the last time,

00:10:14.383 --> 00:10:16.080
why aren't you two together again?

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:19.253
No, I know, I know,

00:10:19.253 --> 00:10:21.670
because you're not in that place.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:24.113
Which would be fine
except you totally are.

00:10:25.282 --> 00:10:27.780
- It's complicated, okay?

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.683
Rachel said she'd marry you?

00:10:31.282 --> 00:10:32.250
- This isn't the right room,

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.450
sorry folks. (audience laughing)

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:36.940
- You are the one who moved
on and didn't tell anyone.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.604
- Oh my god, Ross, this
is just so messed up.

00:10:40.604 --> 00:10:43.380
(sighs) What is wrong with us?

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.930
You know, when people
hear about our situation

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.650
they always ask, you live
together, but you're not a couple?

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:48.750
And you have a baby?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:49.740
Isn't that weird?

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.120
And I say, you know, you know what?

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.320
It's not because it works for us.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.890
But you know what, this doesn't work.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:55.723
Kiss me.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.200
- Rach, it doesn't say that.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.223
- No I'm saying it.

00:11:02.136 --> 00:11:03.736
- But, what-
- Just don't talk.

00:11:05.428 --> 00:11:10.428
(audience cheering)
(Rachel gasping)

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:12.983
Well that's new.

00:11:13.912 --> 00:11:14.910
- You like me?

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:17.704
- Okay, let's not make
a big thing about this.

00:11:17.704 --> 00:11:18.960
- It's a huge thing.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.072
- Okay, not working with me, Joe.

00:11:21.072 --> 00:11:22.390
(audience laughing)

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:25.893
Here's the thing, lately I
have been having thoughts.

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:31.480
Musings, if you will.
(audience laughing)

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:32.650
- For how long?

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.273
- Only like a month.
- A month?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:39.249
- You just went out with
my best friend, you know?

00:11:39.249 --> 00:11:41.749
I just think it would be
a really really bad idea.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:50.123
Or not.
(audience laughing)

00:11:55.422 --> 00:11:58.422
(slow guitar music)

00:12:02.985 --> 00:12:04.620
(audience laughing)

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.453
- Okay.

00:12:05.453 --> 00:12:07.660
Ha ha, you like that, huh?

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:08.640
- Oh yeah.
- You like that.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.018
Let's kick this into high gear, huh?

00:12:11.018 --> 00:12:13.210
(Joey wincing)

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.160
Yeah baby, I'll show you how we do it.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:18.460
- No, no, you kneed me in my misters.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.860
- Well how come Monica
and Chandler could do it?

00:12:27.858 --> 00:12:30.443
- I guess they weren't as
good friends as we are.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.790
- I know I may be way out of bounds here,

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:36.910
but is there any chance
you would take me back?

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:39.940
- Oh god, I am so sorry,

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.303
but I mean,

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.870
there's so much history
between us, you know?

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.673
- The job is in Paris.

00:12:47.839 --> 00:12:51.120
(gentle guitar music)

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.403
- I don't get a goodbye?

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:54.193
- What?

00:12:54.193 --> 00:12:55.900
- Everyone gets a goodbye but me?

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:58.690
What do I gotta do to get a goodbye, huh?

00:12:58.690 --> 00:12:59.966
Be best friends with you?

00:12:59.966 --> 00:13:01.488
Go out with you?

00:13:01.488 --> 00:13:02.850
Have a baby with you?

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:03.683
Oh wait a minute, wait a minute,

00:13:03.683 --> 00:13:04.890
I did all those things.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.980
- Okay, so if you think that
I didn't say goodbye to you

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.750
because you don't mean as
much to me as everybody else,

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:11.890
you're wrong.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.623
It's because you mean more to me.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.770
So there, all right, there's your goodbye.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.120
- Rach!
- What?

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.780
- You can't!

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:21.613
- What?

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:30.280
- We totally did it.
(audience laughing)

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.290
- Oh my god, you and Rachel?

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.330
- I know, it's pretty great.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.300
- So what does that mean?

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:35.820
Are you guys getting back together?

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:37.470
- Oh I don't know.

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:39.250
I mean we didn't really get to talk.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.400
- It's just the perfect
way to say goodbye.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.363
- I don't wanna get over her.

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:47.103
- What?

00:13:47.103 --> 00:13:49.190
- I don't, I wanna be with her.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:50.023
- Really?

00:13:50.023 --> 00:13:51.160
- Yeah, I'm gonna go after her.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:52.033
The thing is,

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.528
don't go.

00:13:55.528 --> 00:13:56.361
- What?

00:13:56.361 --> 00:13:57.840
- Please, please stay with me.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.910
I am so in love with you.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:00.883
Please don't go.

00:14:02.704 --> 00:14:03.800
- Oh my god.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:04.690
- I know, I know,

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.793
I shouldn't have waited til now to say it,

00:14:07.943 --> 00:14:09.720
but that was stupid, okay, I'm sorry.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.053
But I'm telling you now.

00:14:11.915 --> 00:14:14.202
- I can't do this right now, I'm sorry.

00:14:14.202 --> 00:14:15.757
I'm sorry.

00:14:15.757 --> 00:14:16.590
- Rachel.

00:14:17.774 --> 00:14:19.107
- I'm so sorry.

00:14:19.107 --> 00:14:21.480
(answering machine beeping)

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.720
- [Rachel] Ross, hi.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:24.553
It's me.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.910
I just got back on the plane

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.543
and I just feel awful.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.193
That is so not how I wanted
things to end with us.

00:14:36.155 --> 00:14:39.330
It's just that I wasn't
expecting to see you

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.220
and then all of the sudden you're there

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:43.340
and saying these things and...

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:47.600
Now I'm just sitting here and thinking

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:50.313
of all the stuff I should
have said and I didn't.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.080
I mean, I didn't even get to tell you

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.483
that I love you too.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.690
Because of course I do.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:14:59.593
I love you.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:02.443
I love you.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.043
I love you.

00:15:06.846 --> 00:15:07.679
What am I doing?

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:10.153
I love you.

00:15:10.153 --> 00:15:13.295
(audience laughing)

00:15:13.295 --> 00:15:14.900
I've gotta see you.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:16.495
I've gotta get off this plane.

00:15:16.495 --> 00:15:18.777
- Oh my god.
(audience laughing)

00:15:18.777 --> 00:15:19.660
- [Rachel] Excuse me!

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.409
- [Stewardess] Miss, please, sit down.

00:15:21.409 --> 00:15:22.751
(audience laughing)

00:15:22.751 --> 00:15:24.580
- [Rachel] No sorry, but I
need to get off the plane,

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.320
okay, I need to just tell
someone that I love them.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.010
- [Stewardess] Miss, I
can't let you off the plane.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:31.857
- Let her off the plane!
(audience laughing)

00:15:31.857 --> 00:15:33.050
- [Stewardess] I am
afraid you are gonna have

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:33.883
to take your seat.

00:15:33.883 --> 00:15:36.161
- [Rachel] Oh please,
miss, you don't understand.

00:15:36.161 --> 00:15:39.000
- Try to understand!
(audience laughing)

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.870
- [Rachel] Oh come on,
miss, isn't there any way

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.383
that you could just let me off the-

00:15:42.383 --> 00:15:43.216
(beeping)

00:15:43.216 --> 00:15:46.032
- No, no!
(laughing and gasping)

00:15:46.032 --> 00:15:47.930
Oh my god, did she get off the plane?

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.363
Did she get off the plane?

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.643
- I got off the plane.
(audience cheering)

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:05.997
- You got off the plane.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.450
(audience cheering)

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.933
- I do love you.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.380
- I love you too and I'm
never letting you go again.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.730
- Okay, 'cause this is
where I wanna be, okay?

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.330
No more messing around, I
don't wanna mess this up again.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:30.240
- Me neither, okay?

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.400
We are done being stupid.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.580
- Okay.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:34.430
It's you and me, all right?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.270
This is it.
- This is it.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:40.263
Unless we're on a break.
(audience laughing)

00:16:48.592 --> 00:16:53.592
Don't make jokes now.
(audience laughing)

00:16:53.733 --> 00:16:56.816
(audience cheering)

